## Coverity Defect Log

```text
** CID 1688341:       Concurrent data access violations  (MISSING_LOCK)
/src/web/src/web_serve.cpp: 333           in web::WebServer::serve(int, const std::__cxx11::basic_string<char, std::char_traits<char>, std::allocator<char>> &)::[lambda(std::vector<unsigned char, std::allocator<unsigned char>> &, const web::TileFrame &, bool, odb::dbTechLayer *) (instance 1)]::operator ()(std::vector<unsigned char, std::allocator<unsigned char>> &, const web::TileFrame &, bool, odb::dbTechLayer *) const()


_____________________________________________________________________________________________
*** CID 1688341:         Concurrent data access violations  (MISSING_LOCK)
/src/web/src/web_serve.cpp: 333             in web::WebServer::serve(int, const std::__cxx11::basic_string<char, std::char_traits<char>, std::allocator<char>> &)::[lambda(std::vector<unsigned char, std::allocator<unsigned char>> &, const web::TileFrame &, bool, odb::dbTechLayer *) (instance 1)]::operator ()(std::vector<unsigned char, std::allocator<unsigned char>> &, const web::TileFrame &, bool, odb::dbTechLayer *) const()
327           // typed in the browser during a script's pause -- only "Live" draws, at
328           // the user's risk.  Holding renderer_mutex keeps a command from
329           // starting, or resuming from its pause, mid-draw.
330           std::shared_lock<std::shared_mutex> idle;
331           if (!debug_live) {
332             idle = std::shared_lock<std::shared_mutex>(tcl->renderer_mutex);
>>>     CID 1688341:         Concurrent data access violations  (MISSING_LOCK)
>>>     Accessing "this->tcl->running" without holding lock "web::TclEvaluator.renderer_mutex". Elsewhere, "web::TclEvaluator.running" is written to with "TclEvaluator.renderer_mutex" held 3 out of 3 times (1 of these accesses strongly imply that it is necessary).
333             if (tcl->running) {
334               tcl->draw_skipped = true;
335               return;
336             }
337           }
338           seedRendererControls(hook);
```

## Solution

| CID | Defect type | Resolution |
|---|---|---|
| 1688341 | `MISSING_LOCK` | Acquire the deferred renderer shared lock explicitly before reading TclEvaluator::running on non-live draws. |

## Related

- https://github.com/The-OpenROAD-Project/OpenROAD/pull/11683

